  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMuscatine County, Iowa - County Government and Services\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n Search\n \n \n \n\n Menu\n \n \n\n \n\n About \n \n\n Boards & Commissions\n Cemeteries\n Communities\n Elected Officials\n Historic Preservation\n School Districts\n Township Information\n \n \n \n\n Departments \n \n\n Administration Office\n Assessor\n Attorney\n Auditor\n Board of Health\n Board of Supervisors\n Community Services\n Conservation\n County Development\n Emergency Management/911\n Engineer's Office & Highway Department\n General Assistance\n Medical Examiner\n Recorder\n Sheriff\n Treasurer\n Veterans Affairs\n \n \n \n\n Resources \n \n\n Bid Notices\n Calendar\n Careers\n Courts\n Frequently Asked Questions\n News\n Notifications\n \n \n \n\n Contact\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n Search Muscatine County, Iowa\n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n\n\n\n \n\n A place to call home\n \nWelcome to Muscatine County\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Elections \n \n \n\n \n \n Hunting Licenses \n \n \n\n \n \n Meetings \n \n \n\n \n \n Notifications \n \n \n\n \n \n Property Taxes \n \n \n\n \n \n Renew Vehicle Tags \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming Events and Meetings\n \nView All Events\n \n \n\n \n\n \n10/17\n Constellations\n 10:30 am\n 1314 Mulberry Ave. · Muscatine, IA \n\n \nConstellations\n 1314 Mulberry Ave.\n Muscatine, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 17, 2026 \n 10:30 am · 12:00pm \n\nMuscatine County Conservation is partnering with the Muscatine Art Center to bring you Constellations! Learn about the night sky with a presentation, story time, and crafts for children. No registration required. \n \nAges: All Ages \nFor More Information\n \nContact: Michelle Berns \n(563) 264-5922 \n \nPosted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \n10/17\n The Old Barn - Last Open House of the Season\n 11:00 am\n 3300 Cedar St. · Muscatine, IA \n\n \nThe Old Barn - Last Open House of the Season\n 3300 Cedar St.\n Muscatine, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 17, 2026 \n 11:00 am · 3:00pm \n\nTours, informational history boards for the barn ans well as the old county home. Crafts, coloring pages, Trick-or-Treat, and more! Happening rain or shine. An event of the Friends of the Old Barn. \n \nAges: All Ages \nPosted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \n10/17\n Halloween at Saulsbury\n 6:30 pm\n 2007 Saulsbury Road · Muscatine, IA \n\n \nHalloween at Saulsbury\n 2007 Saulsbury Road\n Muscatine, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 17, 2026 \n 6:30 pm · 8:00pm \n\nA fun, entertaining, and safe Halloween event. Visitors will follow a drive through the campground at Saulsbury Bridge Recreation Area where the campsites and other areas will be decorated with a Halloween theme (not scary) by campers. \n \n\nA suggested $10 per vehicle donation will be collected to support the Muscatine County Conservation Foundation. \n \n\nThe first 300 children, 2-12 years of age, will receive a treat bag before they leave the event. \n \n\n  \n \nAges: All ages. \nCost: $10 suggested donation per vehicle \nFor More Information\n \nContact: Michelle Berns \n(563) 264-5922 \nconservation@muscatinecountyiowa.gov \n \nPosted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \n10/19\n Board of Supervisors Meeting\n 9:00 am\n 414 E. 3rd St. · Muscatine, IA \n \n\n \nBoard of Supervisors Meeting\n 414 E. 3rd St.\n Muscatine, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 19, 2026 \n 9:00 am \n\nThe Muscatine County Board of Supervisors typically meets on Mondays at 9:00 a.m. in the board room in the Administration Building, 414 E. 3rd St., Muscatine, IA 52761. \n \n\nWatch live and archived Board of Supervisors meetings on our YouTube channel. \n Agenda \nPosted by: Board of Supervisors \n\n \n \n \n\n \n10/19\n Muscatine County Conservation Board Meeting\n 6:00 pm\n 3300 Cedar St. · Muscatine, IA \n \n\n \nMuscatine County Conservation Board Meeting\n 3300 Cedar St.\n Muscatine, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 19, 2026 \n 6:00 pm \n\nRegular meeting of the Muscatine County Conservation Board. \n \n\nAgenda \n Agenda \nFor More Information\n \nContact: Katie Hammond \nWebsite\n \nPosted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n \n10/24\n Discover Fly Fishing\n 8:00 am\n 3300 Cedar St. · Muscatine, IA \n\n \nDiscover Fly Fishing\n 3300 Cedar St.\n Muscatine, IA\n Map to Event\n \n\n October 24, 2026 \n 8:00 am · 12:00pm \n\nMuscatine County Conservation is partnering with First Watch Fly Co. to offer Fly Casting and Fly Tying Classes designed for beginners and anyone looking to spend intentional time outdoors. \n \n\nJoin us for a hands-on, 4-hour morning session where you will learn the fundamentals of fly fishing in a relaxed, supportive environment. \n \n\nWhat You Will Learn\n \nFly casting fundamentals and techniques\n \nGear setup including rod, reel, line, and leader\n \nIntroduction to reading water\n \nFly tying basics with step-by-step instruction \n \n\nClass Details\n \nDuration: 4-hour morning sessions\n \nSkill Level: Beginner friendly\n \nAll equipment provided (or bring your own) \n \n\nWhether you are new to fly fishing or looking to build your skills, this class is a great way to get started and connect with the outdoors right here in Muscatine County. \n \n\nSpots are limited. Registration required. \n \nCost: Free \nFor More Information\n \n(563) 264-5922 \nConservation@muscatinecountyiowa.gov \n \nPosted by: Conservation \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nNews and Announcements\n \n \n\n \nOctober 13\n \n \n\n Employment\n \n5 Job Openings\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSeptember 29\n \n \n\n Conservation\n \nMuscatine County Conservation Newsletter\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nSeptember 25, 2026\n \n \n\n Conservation\n \nFall & Winter 2026\n \n \n \n \nView All News \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \nStay Informed\n \nCounty Notifications\n \n\n \nBe the first to know about county news, bid notices, employment opportunities, and other key updates by signing up for email alerts about the topics that matter most to you. \n \n \nSign Up for Notifications\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nAbout Muscatine County \n \n\nEstablished in 1836, Muscatine County is a collection of 11 communities and is home to over 42,000 residents. Muscatine, seat of Muscatine County, first came into existence in the summer of 1833 when Colonel George Davenport of Rock Island, Illinois, sent three representatives into the territory to set up a trading post.Muscatine County is administered by a five-member Board of Supervisors, who are elected for four-year terms. Other elected officials include the Attorney, Auditor, Recorder, Sheriff, and Treasurer. \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Administration Building\n 414 E. Third St.\n \nMuscatine, IA 52761 \n \n\n Office Hours\n Monday - Friday \n8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. \nClosed Holidays\n\n Department Hours May Vary\n \n \n\n Contact Us\n Closed Holidays \n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n© 2026 Muscatine County | Accessibility | \nTranslate LanguageTranslate Website\n \npowered by \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \nUpcoming Holiday Closure Schedule\n \n \nVeterans' Day (November 11, 2026)\n \nThanksgiving (November 26, 2026)\n \nDay after Thanksgiving (November 27, 2026)\n \nChristmas Eve (December 24, 2026)\n \nChristmas (December 25, 2026)\n \nNew Years Day (January 1, 2027)\n \nMemorial Day (May 31, 2027)\n \nIndependence Day (July 5, 2027)\n \nLabor Day (September 6, 2027)\n \nVeteran's Day (November 11, 2027)\n \n\n\n"
}
